<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/encyclopedia/conflicts/19th-century">Conflicts &amp; Resolutions</a> · Treaty</p><h1 class="enc-title">Tripartite Convention (1899)</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1899">1899</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/19th-century">19th century</a> · Also known as Tripartite Convention of 1899</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Tripartite Convention of 1899 partitioned the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/samoan-islands">Samoan Islands</a> between <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/germany">Germany</a> and the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/united-states">United States</a>. Signed by Germany, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/britain">Britain</a> and the United States after the Second Samoan Civil War, it gave Germany the western islands of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/upolu">Upolu</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/savaii">Savaiʻi</a> and the United States the eastern islands, including <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tutuila">Tutuila</a>. Britain gave up its claims in return for German concessions in Tonga, the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/solomon">Solomon</a> Islands and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/west-africa">West Africa</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/tripartite-convention-1899.jpg" alt="Tripartite Convention (1899)" width="320" height="262" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Alfred John Tattersall (1861-1951) · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:German,_British,_American_warships_in_Apia_harbour,_Samoa_1899.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
